[Handbook: Melanoma NOS]
•    SSM $(80-85%)$ is the commonest melanoma in Caucasians. Presents as a slowly enlarging, slightly raised, pigmented plaque with irregularity in colour and border. Eventually, a nodule appears within the plaque, indicating deep invasion. Most often on the trunk of men or legs of women (see Fig. 17.10). •    SSM $(80-85\%)$ is the commonest melanoma in Caucasians. Presents as a slowly enlarging, slightly raised, pigmented plaque with irregularity in colour and border. Eventually, a nodule appears within the plaque, indicating deep invasion. Most often on the trunk of men or legs of women (see Fig. 17.10). Table 17.1  Prognosis of malignant melanoma   Table 17.1  Prognosis of malignant melanoma   wzxhzdk:9wzxhzdk:9
